    "cad.summary.dimensions": {
      "comment": "Formatted key. Geometry summary line of a 3D model preview whose length unit is known. Argument 1 is the face count and argument 2 the triangle count, both already formatted for the locale (a face count can read like 100,000+ when the model has more faces than are counted); arguments 3, 4 and 5 are the model width, height and depth, already formatted for the locale; argument 6 is the localized length unit symbol (for example mm or in) that applies to all three dimensions. Keep the six positional placeholders and place the unit after the dimensions the way the language writes units. Approximate tessellated bounds, not certified engineering dimensions. Do not add singular or plural forms: word the labels so they read naturally for any count.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
