    "cad.summary.dimensionsUnitless": {
      "comment": "Formatted key. Geometry summary line of a 3D model preview whose file does not declare a length unit (STL, OBJ and PLY files never do). Arguments 1 and 2 are the face and triangle counts, already formatted for the locale (a face count can read like 100,000+); arguments 3, 4 and 5 are the width, height and depth as plain numbers already formatted for the locale. The closing parenthesis says the numbers have no unit because the file declares none; it must not suggest millimetres or any other unit and must not call the file broken. Keep the five positional placeholders. Approximate tessellated bounds, not certified engineering dimensions.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
