    "finding.certificate.weakKey": {
      "comment": "Safety finding for a certificate file: the number of certificates that use an RSA key shorter than 2,048 bits, which is considered weak. RSA is a technical name and stays as it is. %2$@ is the number of certificates. The count is formatted by the app for the display locale and is never part of the translation. No file content, name or path appears in this sentence. Draft translations pending native-speaker review.",
