    "profile.note.leadingZeros": {
      "comment": "Data-quality note for numeric-looking values that start with zero, such as 007 or a ZIP code. %@ is the locale-formatted count of such values. A spreadsheet that treats the cell as a number would remove the zeros. The sentence is built so the count needs no plural form; keep the count placeholder.",
